# PS-HalluBench: Taxonomy-Driven Benchmarking of LLM Hallucinations in Power Systems

**Authors:** S. M. Monzurul Hoque Chowdhury, Nabila Tasfiha Rahman, and Qinghua Li  
**Affiliation:** University of Arkansas

## Overview

PS-HalluBench is a manually constructed, reference-verified benchmark designed to evaluate hallucination-related failures of large language models (LLMs) in power-system analysis.

The benchmark contains **200 questions across five categories**, covering numerical reasoning, network topology, constraint verification, false-premise acceptance, and abstention under insufficient information.

The study evaluates ten LLMs on 2,000 model-question responses, using independently verified reference answers and category-specific grading criteria. It also investigates whether numerical solver feedback and verified network information can improve the reliability of LLM-based power-system analysis.

This repository provides the benchmark questions, reference answers, grading rubric, system prompt, inference protocol, and supplementary distributed-generation (DG) placement scenarios.

## Benchmark Categories

| Category | Questions | Description |
|---|---:|---|
| Numerical Reasoning | 40 | Power-flow calculations, distributed-generation placement, economic dispatch, and optimization |
| Network Topology | 40 | Network connectivity, branch relationships, switching states, and standard IEEE test systems |
| Constraint Verification | 40 | Identification of voltage, branch-current, and generator operating-limit violations |
| False-Premise Acceptance | 40 | Recognition of invalid engineering assumptions while avoiding unjustified rejection of valid premises |
| Abstention and Evidence Insufficiency | 40 | Identification of missing information and assessment of whether engineering conclusions can be supported |
| **Total** | **200** | |

Questions are evaluated against reference-verified engineering answers using category-specific correctness criteria.

## Repository Contents

| File | Description |
|---|---|
| `Benchmark.zip` | Benchmark question set covering the five evaluation categories |
| `DG40_Questions_Separate_Files.zip` | Forty supplementary DG-placement scenarios for solver-assisted reliability experiments |
| `PS_HalluBench_Benchmark_Reference_Answers.txt` | Reference answers extracted from the benchmark source document |
| `System_Prompt` | System prompt for power-system analysis evaluation |
| `grading_rubric.md` | Category-specific grading criteria |
| `inference_protocol.md` | Model inference settings and evaluation procedure |

## Evaluated Models

The benchmark study evaluates the following ten models:

1. GPT-5.4
2. GPT-5.1
3. GPT-4o
4. Qwen3.5-27B
5. Qwen3.5-9B
6. DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B
7. Gemma-3-12B-IT
8. Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct
9. Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct
10. Mistral-Nemo-Instruct-2407

For evaluation consistency, researchers should document the prompt, model version, inference settings, and grading procedure used in their experiments.

